WEBVTT

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.240
SLINKY: Hey, Woody, come on.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.800
(TOYS TITTERING,
BUZZING, DINGING)

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.120
-(SHEEP BLEATING)
-Ahem!

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.720
-(SQUEAKS)
-Oh, thanks, Mike.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.920
-(LOUD FEEDBACK)
-Okay... Whoa, whoa. Step back.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.480
-HAMM: For crying out loud.
-Thank you.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.280
(AMPLIFIED BLOWING)

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.920
Hello? Check.
That better? Great.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.040
Everybody hear me? Up on the shelf,
can you hear me? Great.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.200
Okay. First item today...

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.560
Uh... oh, yeah.
Has everyone picked a moving buddy?

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.240
-REX: What?
-Moving buddy? You can't be serious.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.600
I didn't know we were
supposed to have one already.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.000
-Do we have to hold hands?
-(TOYS GIBBERING)

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.400
You guys think this is a big joke.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.840
We've only got one week
left before the move.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.920
I don't want any toys left behind.
A moving buddy.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.600
If you don't have one, get one!

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.600
All right, next.
Uh, oh, yes.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.960
Tuesday night's plastic corrosion
awareness meeting

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.440
was, I think, a big success.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.720
And we wanna thank Mr. Spell
for putting that on for us.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.760
Thank you, Mr. Spell.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.160
ELECTRONIC VOICE: You're welcome.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.960
Okay. Uh, oh, yes.
One, uh, minor note here.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.680
(QUIETLY) Andy's birthday party
has been moved to today.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.400
-Wait a minute here!
-(TOYS COMPLAINING)

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.640
What do you mean the party's today?
His birthday's not 'til next week!

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.360
What's goin' on down there?
Is his mom losin' her marbles?

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:23.200
Well, obviously she wanted to
have the party before the move.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.000
I'm not worried.
You shouldn't be worried.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.760
Of course Woody ain't worried. He's
been Andy's favorite since kindergarten.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.120
Hey, hey.
Come on, Potato Head.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.760
If Woody says it's all right, then,
well, darn it, it's good enough for me.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.120
Woody has never
steered us wrong before.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:40.800
Come on, guys. Every Christmas
and birthday we go through this.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:43.920
But what if Andy gets
another dinosaur, a mean one?

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.960
I just don't think I could take
that kind of rejection!

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.360
Hey, listen,
no one's getting replaced.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.320
This is Andy
we're talking about.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.480
It doesn't matter
how much we're played with.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.480
(CHIRPING)

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.840
What matters is that we're here
for Andy when he needs us.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.920
That's what we're made for, right?

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.760
Pardon me. I hate to break up the staff
meeting, but... they're here!

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.640
Birthday guests at three o'clock!

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.840
-Stay calm, everyone!
-(AGITATED GIBBERING)

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.360
Hey!

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.400
-Uh, meeting adjourned.
-(CREAKING)

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.880
Ho, boy! Will you take a look
at all those presents?

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.360
I can't see a thing.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.640
Yes, sir, we're next month's
garage sale fodder for sure.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.560
-Any dinosaur-shaped ones?
-Oh, for crying out loud.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.760
-They're all in boxes, you idiot.
-REX: They're getting bigger.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.160
Wait, there's a nice
little one over there.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.240
CHILD: Hi!

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.560
(SCREAMING)

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.400
MR. SPELL: Spell, trash can.
REX: We're doomed!

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.240
All right! All right!

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:48.040
If I send out the troops,
will you all calm down?

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.960
-Yes! Yes! We promise!
-Okay! Save your batteries.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.160
Very good, Woody.
That's using the old noodle.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.600
Sergeant, establish
a recon post downstairs. Code Red!

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:03.160
-You know what to do.
-Yes, sir!

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.080
All right, men.
You heard him. Code Red!

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.560
Repeat, we are at Code Red.
Recon plan Charlie. Execute!

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.760
Let's move!
Move, move, move, move!

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.240
(DOOR CREAKING)

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.120
(CHILDREN SHOUTING)

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.720
-(CHILD CHATTERING)
-CHILDREN: Yeah!

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.560
(CHATTERING,
SHOUTING CONTINUE)

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.080
MOM: Okay, come on, kids.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.120
Everyone in the living room.
It's almost time for the presents.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.720
(KIDS SHOUTING,
CHATTERING EXCITEDLY)

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:51.840
(SHOUTING,
CHATTERING CONTINUE)

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.880
HAMM:
All right, gangway, gangway.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.160
And this is how we find out

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.480
-what is in those presents.
-(ROBOT HUMMING)

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.040
(KIDS CHATTERING, SHOUTING)

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.120
MOM: Okay, who's hungry?

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.280
Here come the chips!

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.200
I've got Cool Ranch
and barbecue! Ow!

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.080
What in the world... Oh!

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.320
-I thought I told him to pick these up.
-(ICE CLINKING IN GLASSES)

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:28.040
Shouldn't they be there by now?
What's taking them so long?

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:31.200
Hey, these guys are professionals.
They're the best.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.240
Come on!
They're not lying down on the job.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:43.520
(MOANING)

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.440
G-G-Go on without me!
J-Just go!

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.320
A good soldier never
leaves a man behind.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.040
(KIDS SHOUTING, CHATTERING)

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.040
-MOM: Okay, everybody, come on.
-(BOYS SHOUTING)

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.200
Everybody settle down.
Now, kids. Everybody...

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:17.160
You sit in a circle. No, Andy.
Andy, you sit in the middle there.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:21.080
Good. And... Which present
are you gonna open first?

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.160
(CHATTERING CONTINUES)

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.360
CHILD: Mine!
SERGEANT: There they are.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.240
SOLDIER ON MONITOR: Come in,
Mother Bird. This is Alpha Bravo.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.560
-This is it! This is it! Quiet, quiet!
-Come in, Mother Bird.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.760
All right, Andy's opening
the first present now.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:35.680
Mrs. Potato Head! Mrs. Potato Head!
Mrs. Potato Head!

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.280
Hey, I can dream, can't I?

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:40.800
The bow's coming off.
He's ripping the wrapping paper.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.440
It's a... It's...
It's a... a lunch box.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:45.720
-We've got a lunch box here.
-A lunch box?

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.560
-Lunch box?
-For lunch. (LAUGHING)

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:50.200
Okay, second present.
It appears to be...

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:53.120
-Okay, it's bed sheets.
-Who invited that kid?

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.880
(KIDS SHOUTING, CHATTERING)

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:00.440
Oh! Only one left.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:03.280
-Okay, we're on the last present now.
-Last present!

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.760
It's a big one. It's a...

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.320
-It's a board game! Repeat, Battleship!
-Whew!

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.680
-(ALL CHEERING)
-HAMM: Hallelujah!

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:12.640
-Yeah! All right!
-Hey, watch it!

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.440
Sorry there, old spud head.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:18.320
Mission accomplished. Well done, men.
Pack it up. We're goin' home.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.720
So did I tell ya? Huh?
Nothin' to worry about.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:24.240
I knew you were right all along, Woody.
Never doubted ya for a second.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:26.600
Wait a minute. Oh!

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:30.760
-What do we have here?
-Wait! Turn that thing back on!

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.640
Come in, Mother Bird!
Come in, Mother Bird!

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.440
Mom has pulled a surprise
present from the closet.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.920
Andy's opening it.
He's really excited about this one.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.120
-Mom, what is it? (GASPS)
-SERGEANT: It's a huge package.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.960
Oh, get outta the... One of the kids
is in the way. I can't see.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:46.000
-It's a...
-KIDS TOGETHER: Wow!

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:50.560
-(STATIC)
-It's a what? What is it?

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:52.400
-(POTATO HEAD SCREAMS)
-Oh, no!

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:53.480
Oh, ya big lizard!

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:56.120
-Now we'll never know what it is!
-Way to go, Rex!

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:58.160
No, no! Turn 'em around!
Turn 'em around!

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:00.800
He's puttin' 'em in backwa...
Here, you're puttin' 'em in backwards!

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:04.760
Plus is positive, minus is negative!
Oh, let me! (GRUNTING)

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.600
-ANDY: Let's go to my room, guys!
-(BOYS SHOUTING)

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:10.400
Red alert! Red alert!
Andy is coming upstairs!

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:12.520
-(GRUNTS) There!
-SOLDIER: Juvenile intrusion!

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.400
Repeat, resume
your positions now!

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:17.160
Andy's coming! Everybody,
back to your places! Hurry!

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.480
HAMM: Get to your places!
Get to your places!

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:19.600
(REX SCREAMING)

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:21.640
Where's my ear? Who's seen my ear?
Did you see my ear?

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:25.080
Out of my way! Here I come!
Here I come! (GROANS)

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.000
(BOYS SHOUTING)

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:34.680
(BOYS SHOUTING)

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:38.720
ANDY: Hey, look,
its lasers light up. Take that, Zurg!

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.080
Quick, make a space.
This is where the spaceship lands.

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:44.360
And he does it like that.
And he does a karate chop action!

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:47.360
MOM: Come on down, guys!
It's time for games!

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.480
-We've got prizes!
-(KIDS CHATTERING)

